<h2>5&nbsp;&nbsp;Evaluation, Comparison and Critical Analysis</h2>

<h3>5.1&nbsp;&nbsp;Privacy&ndash;utility trade-off of the defences</h3>
<p>For each defence we sweep its strength, running the attack on the defended
gradient (privacy, measured by reconstruction PSNR &mdash; lower is safer) and
training a classifier under the same mechanism (utility, measured by test
accuracy). A strong defence pushes PSNR down while holding accuracy up.</p>
<div class="fig"><img src="{{PU_IMG}}" style="max-width:92%"><div class="cap">Privacy&ndash;utility trade-off for each defence (Modules 2, 3, 5). Blue = test accuracy; red = reconstruction PSNR.</div></div>
